{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-11T19:21:05.266Z","data":{"text":"The task is complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n## Implementation\n\n**`src/core/web/web-tree-hub.ts`** (new) — exports `createTreeHub(options): Promise<InvalidationHub>`. It:\n- Resolves the change trees through its `trees` seam (default `changeTrees`) and the tree record path through `treeRecordPath` at startup, and opens a `createInvalidationHub` over both (OpenSpec root of the first tree, each worktree tree's change folder, and the record path).\n- Forwards each inner batch to its own subscribers, then re-resolves the trees. When `treeWatchPaths` differ it opens a hub over the new trees with the same record path, closes the old hub, and emits one `{ ids: [] }` batch — clients stay connected because the outer hub never swaps.\n- Runs resolutions one at a time (with one queued follow-up); a failed resolution keeps the current hub.\n- Polls every `inbox.pollSeconds` through its `every` seam; the default is an `unref()`ed `setInterval`.\n- `cancelPending` cancels the current hub's pending batch; `close` cancels the poll, closes the hub, and drops subscribers.\n- Reuses `TreesFn`/`EveryFn` from `dispatch-watch.ts` via type-only imports; carries `@scenario web-inspection:`/`@adr 013` tags and stays within the 80-line function budget.\n\n**`src/core/web/web-server.ts`** — `startWebServer` now builds its hub with `createTreeHub`, passing `serve.eventDebounceMs` and its `watch`, `schedule`, `trees`, `every` seams; the direct `changeTrees` call and `createInvalidationHub` use are gone; `WebServerOptions` gains optional `trees` and `every`. File is 247 lines (budget 250), `startWebServer` still spans 158 lines.\n\n**`tests/serve-tree-hub.test.ts`** (new) — proves all five scenarios with `scenario('web-inspection', ...)` (Tree record in the server's watch, Tree record change, New worktree while serving, Poll finds a new worktree, Server closes the poll) using a fake watcher, manual schedule and every seams, a temp git repo with `vcs.enabled`, and real SSE clients, plus `it` tests for the unref'd default poll and `cancelPending`.\n\n## Verification\n- Task verify (`node --import tsx --import ./tests/git-test-env.ts --test tests/serve-tree-hub.test.ts tests/serve-sse-worktrees.test.ts`): 10/10 pass, `serve-sse-worktrees.test.ts` unchanged.\n- Proposal verify (`pnpm verify`): typecheck cli/ui, build, all 169 tests, and lint all pass."}}
